course: dictionary
lesson: 3849
title: One word, two meanings: found
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Found has two jobs. Most often it is the past of find: «I found my keys under the sofa.» Here found means discovered something that was lost or hidden.
explain: The other job is to start something new, like a school, a city or a company: «She founded a charity.» Look at the clues. Did someone discover a thing, or did someone set something up? The words around found tell you which.
explain: Found can also be an adjective, as in «lost and found», the box at school where lost jumpers wait to be claimed. A quick test: swap in a meaning. If «start» fits, it is the second job. If «discover» fits, it is the first.
fact: Found, the past of find, means discovered something that was lost or hidden.
fact: To found something means to start or set it up, such as a school, a city or a company.
fact: «LEGO is a Danish company founded in 1932.» The company was started in 1932.
fact: The person who starts something is called its founder.
fact: «The Qing dynasty, 1644–1912, was founded by the Manchus from the northeast.» The Manchus started the Qing dynasty.
exercise: «I found my keys under the sofa.» What does found mean here? | *Discovered something that was lost | Painted the front door | Started a new company | Carried a heavy box
exercise: «The Manchus founded the Qing dynasty.» What does founded mean? | Sang a long song | Broke into pieces | *Started or set up | Looked for something lost
exercise: Jayden sees a sign in school: «Lost and found». What does found mean on this sign? | Things that are being searched for right now | Things that are for sale | *Things that were lost and have been found | Things that were started long ago
test: «She ___ a charity to help animals.» (meaning: set up) | fined | found the box | finding | *founded
test: «Ravi ___ his lost watch behind the radiator.» (meaning: discovered) | *found | founder | fond | founded
exam: «A legend says three brothers and their sister founded the city.» What does founded mean here? | *Set up or started | Discovered after a long search | Ruined by floods | Lost for ever
